  "comment": "Single source of truth for parity scenes. tools/generate_scenes.py turns this into tools/bullet_scenes.h (C++) and crates/bullet/src/parity_scenes.rs (Rust); do not edit the generated files. Scenes must be reproducible: fixed dt (as a fraction), fixed iterations, deterministic shapes/poses. 'record' lists the bodies whose trajectories are compared. Shape types: box(half_extents), sphere(radius), capsule/cylinder/cone(radius, half_height), plane(normal, constant), mesh(grid[nx,nz], origin[x0,z0], cell[dx,dz], heights[nx*nz] in z-major order; indices derived with the falling_mesh winding). Body fields: mass (0 = static), friction, restitution, position, optional velocity[vx,vy,vz] (initial linear velocity) and ccd{motion_threshold, swept_sphere_radius}. Consumer-API body fields (all optional): gravity[x,y,z] (implies DISABLE_WORLD_GRAVITY: the body keeps its own gravity detached from world propagation), no_contact_response (true = trigger/sensor, CF_NO_CONTACT_RESPONSE), group/mask (collision filter group & mask, -1 = all; default group 1 / mask -1). Consumer-API scene fields (optional): pair_filter [nameA, nameB] (this pair is excluded from collision, btOverlapFilterCallback style), rays [{from, to, mode 'all'|'closest', group, mask}] (probed once after the last frame, recorded to <scene>_rays_*.csv: ray_idx body_idx fraction, sorted by fraction).",
